Cell["\<\
path is a list of reciprocal-fractional line segments and endpoint labels. \
npoint controls the sampling of each segment.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"29aa2d2f-2175-43d1-8c08-4b9aa95d9954"],

Cell["\<\
Every symbol in H other than kx, ky, and kz becomes an interactive parameter. \
The sliders start at zero, so the initial plot may show coincident flat bands \
when all Hamiltonian parameters vanish.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f54c008c-d7c0-4acf-b30c-d7865a412c71"],

Cell["\<\
Use standardKPath[] as the first argument when MagneticTB should choose the \
built-in conventional path from the current initialized lattice. \
bandManipulate receives the explicit path returned by standardKPath[].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1679852a-42c5-44ca-9fbb-1ec9c2c5c50d"],

Cell["\<\
No energy shift is added. For a genuinely non-Hermitian Hamiltonian, choose \
explicitly whether to plot the real part, imaginary part, or complex spectrum \
before calling this function.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c0cca7dd-8ee7-44d4-8db4-2204607f96a4"]
}, Closed]],

